diff --git a/docs/numerics.md b/docs/numerics.md
index efcb36b..d803b56 100644
--- a/docs/numerics.md
+++ b/docs/numerics.md
@@ -1533,3 +1533,35 @@ and both E and outputs are `[steps][4][groups]`. Horner and source scaling have
 contract above. Zero steps/groups writes nothing. With zero terms, E is still multiplied
 by canonical zero, preserving statuses. Outputs contain sources in ascending step order;
 the consumer chooses their application order.
+
+## Experimental per-product Gauss GEMM (unreleased)
+
+The isolated P1.3 prototype `gemm_gauss` is not part of a published API. It accepts
+complex `StridedGemm` inputs and the existing host/resident layouts, broadcast,
+accumulation and final negation rules. `fused=true` is rejected. Existing GEMM calls
+and defaults are unchanged. Any accepted addition requires a minor release.
+
+At each ascending inner index, with RN the precision-B ties-to-even operation:
+
+```
+p = RN(ar * br)
+q = RN(ai * bi)
+s = RN(RN(ar + ai) * RN(br + bi))
+r = RN(p - q)
+i = RN(RN(s - p) - q)
+acc_re = RN(r + acc_re)
+acc_im = RN(i + acc_im)
+```
+
+Start each accumulator from zero or its corresponding C component. Negate both
+components after the complete dot when requested. Status propagation follows each
+scalar operation in this sequence. Output padding is preserved. Empty dots still
+apply accumulation and final negation. This differs from composing the usual four
+real products and from the matrix-level Gauss experiment, which first accumulates
+three separate real dots and reconstructs each complex entry only once afterward.
+Cancellation can magnify the rounded input sums and reconstruction error.
+
+The native shader computes three real products once per complex entry and keeps
+private significands padded to 33 storage words at logical precision N. It uses
+no new public buffer layout. This new compiler context needs independent MPFR,
+all-width dense/wide/shader checks and broad regressions before timing or acceptance.
